IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`

-- wra3-pt4-s92.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, section 92(3) (definitions for the power to make
-- supplementary and consequential provision in relation to Part 4). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt,
-- a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- Only subsection (3) is encoded here. Subsections (1) and (2) are a regulation-making power (inert, reason 2); the two
-- definitions say what "primary legislation" and "secondary legislation" mean in that power, and they are closed definitions
-- ("means"), so a kind of legislation they do not name is outside them.

§ `s 92(3) primary legislation and secondary legislation`

DECLARE `s 92(3) legislation` IS ONE OF
    `s 92(3) an Act`
    `s 92(3) an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `s 92(3) an instrument made under primary legislation`
    `s 92(3) any other legislation`

-- src:1488 | (a) “primary legislation” means an Act or Act of the Scottish Parliament;
@ref s 92(3)(a) primary legislation (src:1488)
GIVEN `the legislation` IS A `s 92(3) legislation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(3)(a) the legislation is primary legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the legislation`
    WHEN `s 92(3) an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 92(3) an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“primary legislation” means an Act or Act of the Scottish Parliament" (a closed definition)
    WHEN `s 92(3) an instrument made under primary legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“primary legislation” means an Act or Act of the Scottish Parliament" (a closed definition)
    WHEN `s 92(3) any other legislation` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:1489 | (b) “secondary legislation” means any instrument made under primary legislation.
@ref s 92(3)(b) secondary legislation (src:1489)
GIVEN `the legislation` IS A `s 92(3) legislation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(3)(b) the legislation is secondary legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the legislation`
    WHEN `s 92(3) an instrument made under primary legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“secondary legislation” means any instrument made under primary legislation" (a closed definition)
    WHEN `s 92(3) an Act` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“secondary legislation” means any instrument made under primary legislation" (a closed definition)
    WHEN `s 92(3) an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“secondary legislation” means any instrument made under primary legislation" (a closed definition)
    WHEN `s 92(3) any other legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
